{"parentUuid":"729e9d0d-6497-4f0d-9fbf-9a1b299ef2ce","isSidechain":true,"userType":"external","cwd":"/root","sessionId":"13e7ab6f-ed04-46aa-b9d9-5671a1da470b","version":"2.1.19","gitBranch":"","agentId":"ae06797","slug":"sprightly-baking-marble","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_vrtx_01SJ7dRQ1pQkb4QgUArQa8aN","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"SimPO Simple Preference Optimization loss function formula 2024\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"[2405.14734] SimPO: Simple Preference Optimization with a Reference-Free Reward\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2405.14734\"},{\"title\":\"SimPO: Simple Preference Optimization with a Reference-Free Reward Yu Meng1∗\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2405.14734\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - princeton-nlp/SimPO: [NeurIPS 2024] SimPO: Simple Preference Optimization with a Reference-Free Reward\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/princeton-nlp/SimPO\"},{\"title\":\"SimPO: Simple Preference Optimization with a Reference-Free Reward | alphaXiv\",\"url\":\"https://www.alphaxiv.org/overview/2405.14734v3\"},{\"title\":\"Simple Preference Optimization (SimPO)\",\"url\":\"https://www.emergentmind.com/topics/simple-preference-optimization-simpo\"},{\"title\":\"SimPO: simple preference optimization with a reference- ...\",\"url\":\"https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.5555/3737916.3741862\"},{\"title\":\"SimPO: Simple Preference Optimization with a Reference-Free Reward | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/forum?id=3Tzcot1LKb\"},{\"title\":\"Paper page - SimPO: Simple Preference Optimization with a Reference-Free Reward\",\"url\":\"https://huggingface.co/papers/2405.14734\"},{\"title\":\"SimPO: Simple Preference Optimization with a Reference-Free Reward | Zihao Tang’s Homepage\",\"url\":\"https://ishikura-a.github.io/paper_reading/2024/06/02/SimPO.html\"},{\"title\":\"[PDF] SimPO: Simple Preference Optimization with a Reference-Free Reward | Semantic Scholar\",\"url\":\"https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/SimPO:-Simple-Preference-Optimization-with-a-Reward-Meng-Xia/c3f1fae241a3c2449e675ab750873d800f95513c\"}]\n\nI found comprehensive information about SimPO (Simple Preference Optimization). Here are the key details about the loss function formula:\n\n## SimPO Overview\n\nSimPO is a simpler yet more effective approach to preference optimization, with effectiveness attributed to using the average log probability of a sequence as the implicit reward.(no content)This reward formulation eliminates the need for a reference model, making it more compute and memory efficient.\n\n## Loss Function Formula\n\nThe objective function of SimPO is derived using NLL (Negative Log Likelihood) loss: L_SimPO(π_θ) = -E_{(x,y_w,y_l)~D}[log σ(p(y_w ≻ y_l|x))].\n\nThe key components are:\n\n1. **Length-normalized reward**: r_SimPO(x,y) = β · p_θ(y|x), where β is a constant that controls the scaling of the reward difference.\n\n2. **Target reward margin**: A target reward margin term γ>0 is introduced to the Bradley-Terry objective to ensure that the reward for the winning response r(x,y_w) exceeds the reward for the losing response r(x,y_l) by at least γ: p(y_w ≻ y_l|x) = σ(r(x,y_w) - r(x,y_l) - γ).\n\n## Performance\n\nSimPO outperforms DPO by up to 6.4 points on AlpacaEval 2 and by up to 7.5 points on Arena-Hard, with the top-performing Gemma-2-9B-it model achieving a 72.4% length-controlled win rate on AlpacaEval 2.\n\nThe paper was submitted on May 23, 2024 and accepted at NeurIPS 2024.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"d9051bd2-17c7-4675-9211-ef9b19deef2b","timestamp":"2026-01-29T06:54:08.855Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"729e9d0d-6497-4f0d-9fbf-9a1b299ef2ce"}
