{"parentUuid":"960da666-964c-42ec-a8fd-c3d51c182dcd","isSidechain":true,"userType":"external","cwd":"/root","sessionId":"13e7ab6f-ed04-46aa-b9d9-5671a1da470b","version":"2.1.19","gitBranch":"","agentId":"ae06797","slug":"sprightly-baking-marble","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_vrtx_019Ahwh5YKn6e5JWXmzpUugw","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"SimPO loss formula beta gamma average log probability Bradley-Terry\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"SimPO: Simple Preference Optimization with a Reference-Free Reward | alphaXiv\",\"url\":\"https://www.alphaxiv.org/overview/2405.14734v3\"},{\"title\":\"SimPO: Simple Preference Optimization with a Reference-Free Reward | Zihao Tang’s Homepage\",\"url\":\"https://ishikura-a.github.io/paper_reading/2024/06/02/SimPO.html\"},{\"title\":\"torchtune.rlhf.loss.dpo — torchtune 0.5 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://pytorch.org/torchtune/0.5/_modules/torchtune/rlhf/loss/dpo.html\"},{\"title\":\"Bradley–Terry model - Wikipedia\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bradley%E2%80%93Terry_model\"},{\"title\":\"Bradley-Terry Models in R\",\"url\":\"https://cran.r-project.org/web/packages/BradleyTerry2/vignettes/BradleyTerry.html\"},{\"title\":\"Real-statistics\",\"url\":\"https://real-statistics.com/reliability/bradley-terry-model/\"},{\"title\":\"Lecture 24 — The Bradley-Terry model\",\"url\":\"https://web.stanford.edu/class/archive/stats/stats200/stats200.1172/Lecture24.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"[PDF] SimPO: Simple Preference Optimization with a Reference-Free Reward | Semantic Scholar\",\"url\":\"https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/SimPO:-Simple-Preference-Optimization-with-a-Reward-Meng-Xia/c3f1fae241a3c2449e675ab750873d800f95513c\"},{\"title\":\"Bradley-Terry Model | Kaggle - Men’s March Madness 2019\",\"url\":\"https://youhoo0521.github.io/kaggle-march-madness-men-2019/models/bradley_terry.html\"},{\"title\":\"Eﬃcient Bayesian Inference for Generalized Bradley-Terry Models Fran¸cois Caron\",\"url\":\"https://www.stats.ox.ac.uk/~doucet/caron_doucet_bayesianbradleyterry.pdf\"}]\n\nI found detailed information about the SimPO loss formula. Here's what the search revealed:\n\n## SimPO Loss Formula\n\nSimPO uses the average log probability of a sequence as the implicit reward, with the reward defined as r_SimPO(x,y) = β · p_θ(y|x), where β is a constant that controls the scaling of the reward difference.\n\n### Key Parameters:\n\n- **Beta (β)**: Equivalent temperature scaling parameter to DPO loss, typically in the range of 2.0 to 2.5\n\n- **Gamma (γ)**: Target reward margin hyperparameter, typically γ ∈ (0, 1.5], with default value of 0.5\n\n### Bradley-Terry Objective with Margin:\n\nSimPO introduces a target reward margin term γ > 0 to the Bradley-Terry objective to ensure that the reward for the winning response r(x,y_w) exceeds the reward for the losing response r(x,y_l) by at least γ: p(y_w ≻ y_l|x) = σ(r(x,y_w) - r(x,y_l) - γ)\n\n### Key Features:\n\nThe reward directly uses the average log probability of tokens in a response under the current policy model, eliminating dependence on a reference model. The length normalization (division by |y|) is crucial for preventing the model from exploiting response length to achieve higher rewards.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"41cfa549-4f4b-47b6-b8dc-2c2531574b44","timestamp":"2026-01-29T06:54:32.802Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"960da666-964c-42ec-a8fd-c3d51c182dcd"}
