{"parentUuid":"307d7b8b-4a8c-49ce-a69a-054b50fd798d","isSidechain":true,"userType":"external","cwd":"/root","sessionId":"13e7ab6f-ed04-46aa-b9d9-5671a1da470b","version":"2.1.19","gitBranch":"","agentId":"ae06797","slug":"sprightly-baking-marble","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929","id":"msg_vrtx_01EwBrknj8FjMYE2EUJUviqN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_vrtx_01BTjfsiWDspLGf1rCdcrAg4","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://www.alphaxiv.org/overview/2405.14734v3","prompt":"Extract the complete SimPO loss formula including the mathematical equation with beta, gamma, and how the loss is computed from policy_chosen_logps and policy_rejected_logps"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":152,"cache_read_input_tokens":58931,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":152,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":24}},"requestId":"req_vrtx_011CXbEKYLfDtgbWgD7GVjbw","type":"assistant","uuid":"44824984-daf2-4795-8cb2-9707a956fa80","timestamp":"2026-01-29T06:54:39.640Z"}
{"parentUuid":"44824984-daf2-4795-8cb2-9707a956fa80","isSidechain":true,"userType":"external","cwd":"/root","sessionId":"13e7ab6f-ed04-46aa-b9d9-5671a1da470b","version":"2.1.19","gitBranch":"","agentId":"ae06797","slug":"sprightly-baking-marble","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_vrtx_01BTjfsiWDspLGf1rCdcrAg4","type":"tool_result","content":"# SimPO Loss Formula\n\nBased on the document, the complete SimPO loss function is:\n\n$$L_{SimPO}(\\pi_\\theta) = -E_{(x,y_w,y_l)\\sim D} \\left[ \\log\\sigma \\left( \\beta\\frac{1}{|y_w|}\\log\\pi_\\theta(y_w|x) - \\beta\\frac{1}{|y_l|}\\log\\pi_\\theta(y_l|x) - \\gamma \\right) \\right]$$\n\n## Key Components:\n\n- **β**: Temperature parameter scaling the rewards\n- **γ**: Target reward margin encouraging separation between preferred and dispreferred responses\n- **|y|**: Response length for normalization\n- **π_θ**: Current policy model\n\n## Computation:\n\nThe loss contrasts length-normalized log probabilities of chosen versus rejected responses. The formula computes: \"using the average log probability of a sequence as the implicit reward\" with margin γ applied to the Bradley-Terry preference objective.\n\nThis eliminates the reference model dependency present in DPO while directly aligning training with generation metrics (average log probability). The document indicates SimPO achieves improvements of \"up to 6.4 points on AlpacaEval 2 and by up to 7.5 points on Arena-Hard\" compared to DPO."}]},"uuid":"aa7569a5-5e4b-48b9-81f6-f4e2b9d0410a","timestamp":"2026-01-29T06:54:45.147Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"44824984-daf2-4795-8cb2-9707a956fa80"}
