{"parentUuid":"28a53e2d-d738-4751-8bd5-07f6fef29d5e","isSidechain":true,"userType":"external","cwd":"/root","sessionId":"13e7ab6f-ed04-46aa-b9d9-5671a1da470b","version":"2.1.19","gitBranch":"","agentId":"ae06797","slug":"sprightly-baking-marble","type":"progress","data":{"type":"search_results_received","resultCount":3,"query":"\"SimPO\" implementation \"policy_chosen_logps\" \"policy_rejected_logps\" pytorch code"},"toolUseID":"srvtoolu_vrtx_01LoA4Btf8zpWM2SViZSfZrH","parentToolUseID":"toolu_vrtx_01Qg2ZWCJ8BdgvcK9NzyMi3t","uuid":"dcdaea67-23fe-4ccd-a304-eeb8064c13f1","timestamp":"2026-01-29T06:54:50.713Z"}
{"parentUuid":"a2c4737e-0a73-46c7-9b0b-f7d9521d4f3b","isSidechain":true,"userType":"external","cwd":"/root","sessionId":"13e7ab6f-ed04-46aa-b9d9-5671a1da470b","version":"2.1.19","gitBranch":"","agentId":"ae06797","slug":"sprightly-baking-marble","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_vrtx_01Qg2ZWCJ8BdgvcK9NzyMi3t","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"SimPO\" implementation \"policy_chosen_logps\" \"policy_rejected_logps\" pytorch code\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"SimPOLoss — torchtune 0.4 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://pytorch.org/torchtune/stable/generated/torchtune.rlhf.loss.SimPOLoss.html\"},{\"title\":\"Source code for torchtune.rlhf.loss.dpo\",\"url\":\"https://docs.pytorch.org/torchtune/0.4/_modules/torchtune/rlhf/loss/dpo.html\"},{\"title\":\"torchtune.rlhf.loss.dpo — torchtune 0.5 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://www.aidoczh.com/torchtune/_modules/torchtune/rlhf/loss/dpo.html\"}]\n\nI found information about SimPO implementation in PyTorch. Here are the key findings:\n\n## SimPO Implementation in PyTorch\n\nSimPO is nearly identical to DPO but uses average logprobs to eliminate the need for a reference model to regularize the policy during training, and also uses a target reward margin to guide the policy towards better responses.\n\n### Code Implementation\n\nThe SimPO loss function takes two main parameters: `policy_chosen_logps` (average log probabilities of the policy model for the chosen responses with shape [b,]) and `policy_rejected_logps` (average log probabilities of the policy model for the rejected responses with shape [b,]).\n\nThe implementation is available in **PyTorch's torchtune library** as `SimPOLoss`. The loss accepts parameters including beta (temperature scaling, typically 2.0-2.5, default 2.0), gamma (target reward margin hyperparameter, typically in (0, 1.5], default 0.5), and label_smoothing (default 0).\n\n### Key Resources:\n- **Official PyTorch Documentation**: https://pytorch.org/torchtune/stable/generated/torchtune.rlhf.loss.SimPOLoss.html\n- **Source Code**: https://docs.pytorch.org/torchtune/0.4/_modules/torchtune/rlhf/loss/dpo.html\n- **Paper Reference**: https://arxiv.org/abs/2405.14734\n\nThe implementation can be found in the `torchtune.rlhf.loss` module and is based on the TRL (Transformer Reinforcement Learning) implementation.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"44ee42e6-9dda-4b90-8703-bfac538082c5","timestamp":"2026-01-29T06:54:57.720Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"a2c4737e-0a73-46c7-9b0b-f7d9521d4f3b"}
