{"parentUuid":"cbda0414-2f0c-471c-aa1d-e9a51230fbc2","isSidechain":true,"userType":"external","cwd":"/root","sessionId":"13e7ab6f-ed04-46aa-b9d9-5671a1da470b","version":"2.1.19","gitBranch":"","agentId":"ae06797","slug":"sprightly-baking-marble","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_vrtx_015DCyBdatWSok4Wm7aKqzb7","type":"tool_result","content":"/root/SimPO/scripts/simpo_trainer.py\n/root/SimPO/scripts/simpo_config.py\n/root/SimPO/unit_test/unit_test_1.py","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"6fca1580-d739-4982-bd75-2fc6c9d6d70e","timestamp":"2026-01-29T06:55:33.800Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"cbda0414-2f0c-471c-aa1d-e9a51230fbc2"}
{"parentUuid":"6fca1580-d739-4982-bd75-2fc6c9d6d70e","isSidechain":true,"userType":"external","cwd":"/root","sessionId":"13e7ab6f-ed04-46aa-b9d9-5671a1da470b","version":"2.1.19","gitBranch":"","agentId":"ae06797","slug":"sprightly-baking-marble","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929","id":"msg_vrtx_019WKSzhS8HBfqdYg3bKmNo3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now let me create a comprehensive summary based on all the information I've gathered from the code, documentation, and research.\n\n## Summary: SimPO Loss Function Formula and Implementation Details\n\nBased on my analysis of the SimPO codebase at `/root/SimPO` and research into the SimPO paper, here's what I found:\n\n### 1. The Exact Mathematical Formula for SimPO Loss\n\nThe complete SimPO loss function is:\n\n```\nL_SimPO(π_θ) = -E[(x,y_w,y_l)~D] [ log σ( β · (1/|y_w|) · log π_θ(y_w|x) - β · (1/|y_l|) · log π_θ(y_l|x) - γ ) ]\n```\n\nWhere:\n- `σ` is the sigmoid function\n- `π_θ` is the current policy model\n- `(x, y_w, y_l)` represents a prompt x with winning response y_w and losing response y_l\n- `|y|` is the response length (number of tokens)\n\n**In simpler terms:**\n```python\nlosses = -log(sigmoid(beta * policy_chosen_logps - beta * policy_rejected_logps - gamma))\n```\n\n### 2. What Beta (β) and Gamma (γ) Parameters Represent\n\n**Beta (β):**\n- **Purpose**: Temperature scaling parameter that controls the scaling of the reward difference\n- **Typical values**: 2.0 to 10.0 (SimPO requires much larger β than DPO)\n- **Effect**: Larger β amplifies the difference between chosen and rejected rewards\n- **In code** (from `/root/SimPO/scripts/simpo_config.py`): Default value is `beta: float = 2.0`\n- **From README**: \"SimPO requires a much larger `beta` than DPO. In our preprint, we used a beta of `2.0` or `2.5`, but in many cases, an even larger beta (e.g., `10`) could yield better results.\"\n\n**Gamma (γ):**\n- **Purpose**: Target reward margin that ensures the reward for winning response exceeds losing response by at least γ\n- **Typical values**: 0 to 1.5, with common values being 0.5\n- **Effect**: Creates a margin in the preference objective to encourage clearer separation between chosen and rejected responses\n- **In code**: The implementation uses `gamma_beta_ratio` instead of γ directly\n  - `gamma = beta * gamma_beta_ratio`\n  - Default: `gamma_beta_ratio: float = 0.25`\n  - So default γ = 2.0 * 0.25 = 0.5\n\n**From README**: \"We suggest tuning the ratio of gamma to beta (i.e., `gamma / beta`). We recommend using `0.5` as a starting point for `gamma_beta_ratio` and grid searching between `0` and `1`.\"\n\n### 3. How the Loss is Computed from policy_chosen_logps and policy_rejected_logps\n\nFrom the code at `/root/SimPO/scripts/simpo_trainer.py` (lines 560-577), the `simpo_loss` function signature shows:\n\n```python\ndef simpo_loss(\n    self,\n    policy_chosen_logps: torch.FloatTensor,  # Shape: (batch_size,)\n    policy_rejected_logps: torch.FloatTensor,  # Shape: (batch_size,)\n) -> Tuple[torch.FloatTensor, torch.FloatTensor, torch.FloatTensor]:\n    \"\"\"Compute the SimPO loss for a batch of policy model log probabilities.\n    \n    Returns:\n        A tuple of three tensors: (losses, chosen_rewards, rejected_rewards).\n    \"\"\"\n```\n\n**The computation steps are:**\n\n1. **Input**: `policy_chosen_logps` and `policy_rejected_logps` are **average log probabilities** per sequence (already length-normalized)\n   - These are computed by the `get_batch_logps` method with `average_log_prob=True` (line 614)\n   - Formula: `sum(log_probs) / number_of_tokens`\n\n2. **Compute rewards**:\n   ```python\n   chosen_rewards = beta * policy_chosen_logps\n   rejected_rewards = beta * policy_rejected_logps\n   ```\n\n3. **Compute loss**:\n   ```python\n   gamma = beta * gamma_beta_ratio\n   logits = chosen_rewards - rejected_rewards - gamma\n   losses = -F.logsigmoid(logits)\n   ```\n\n### 4. What chosen_rewards and rejected_rewards Should Be\n\n**Chosen Rewards:**\n```python\nchosen_rewards = beta * policy_chosen_logps\n```\n- This is β times the average log probability of the chosen response\n- Shape: `(batch_size,)`\n- **Key insight**: Uses the **average** log probability (sum of log probs divided by sequence length) as the implicit reward, eliminating the need for a reference model\n\n**Rejected Rewards:**\n```python\nrejected_rewards = beta * policy_rejected_logps\n```\n- This is β times the average log probability of the rejected response  \n- Shape: `(batch_size,)`\n\n**Important Note**: The crucial difference from DPO is that SimPO uses **length-normalized** log probabilities (averaged over sequence length). This is handled automatically by the `get_batch_logps` method when called with `average_log_prob=True` at line 614:\n\n```python\nall_logps = self.get_batch_logps(\n    all_logits,\n    concatenated_batch[\"concatenated_labels\"],\n    average_log_prob=True,  # This normalizes by length\n    is_encoder_decoder=self.is_encoder_decoder,\n    label_pad_token_id=self.label_pad_token_id,\n)\n```\n\n### Key Implementation Files:\n\n1. **`/root/SimPO/scripts/simpo_trainer.py`**: Main trainer with `simpo_loss` method (line 560)\n2. **`/root/SimPO/scripts/simpo_config.py`**: Configuration with beta and gamma_beta_ratio parameters (lines 55-56)\n3. **`/root/SimPO/README.md`**: Hyperparameter tuning guidelines\n\n### Complete Loss Implementation (Pseudocode):\n\n```python\ndef simpo_loss(policy_chosen_logps, policy_rejected_logps):\n    # policy_chosen_logps and policy_rejected_logps are already averaged over sequence length\n    \n    gamma = self.beta * self.gamma_beta_ratio\n    \n    # Compute rewards (length-normalized implicit rewards)\n    chosen_rewards = self.beta * policy_chosen_logps\n    rejected_rewards = self.beta * policy_rejected_logps\n    \n    # Compute preference logits with margin\n    logits = chosen_rewards - rejected_rewards - gamma\n    \n    # Apply negative log sigmoid (equivalent to binary cross-entropy)\n    losses = -F.logsigmoid(logits)\n    \n    return losses, chosen_rewards, rejected_rewards\n```\n\n### Sources:\n- [SimPO Paper on arXiv](https://arxiv.org/abs/2405.14734)\n- [SimPO GitHub Repository](https://github.com/princeton-nlp/SimPO)\n- [AlphaXiv Overview](https://www.alphaxiv.org/overview/2405.14734v3)\n- [PyTorch Torchtune Documentation](https://pytorch.org/torchtune/stable/generated/torchtune.rlhf.loss.SimPOLoss.html)\n- [Torchtune GitHub Issues](https://github.com/pytorch/torchtune/issues/2206)"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":216,"cache_read_input_tokens":62265,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":216,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1}},"requestId":"req_vrtx_011CXbEPmtMoCUkPVqystzrr","type":"assistant","uuid":"9c57e86f-99e6-4d3c-97e9-5f0e6023a739","timestamp":"2026-01-29T06:56:09.172Z"}
